/**
 * @defgroup EcalGeo EcalGeo — Endcap EMC Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR Endcap Electromagnetic Calorimeter (EEMC)
 *
 * @details
 * The EEMC (detector tag **ECAL**) is a lead–polystyrene sampling calorimeter mounted on
 * the west pole-tip face of the STAR solenoidal magnet.  It covers 1.086 < η < 2.0 with
 * full azimuth, extending the electromagnetic acceptance of the experiment beyond the
 * barrel BEMC.  The detector is divided into two identical half-wheels, each spanning
 * 180° in φ, assembled from 6 azimuthal supersectors of 5 slices each (30 sectors total).
 *
 * ### Longitudinal structure
 * The calorimeter is segmented into five readout sections in z (total depth 41.244 cm):
 * - **Sections 1, 2** — 1 scintillator layer each, cell width 1.505 cm
 * - **Section 3** — 4 scintillator layers, cell width 1.405 cm
 * - **Section 4** — 18 scintillator layers, cell width 1.405 cm (main shower sampling)
 * - **Section 5** — 1 scintillator layer, cell width 1.505 cm (post-shower)
 *
 * Lead absorbers (0.457 cm) are clad on both sides with 0.05 cm stainless steel.
 * A 0.953 cm aluminium front plate completes the support structure.
 *
 * ### Shower Maximum Detector (SMD)
 * A scintillator-strip SMD is located at z = 279.542 cm within the 3.4 cm gap between
 * sections 3 and 4.  Triangular strips (apex 0.7 cm, base 1.0 cm) are arranged in two
 * orthogonal planes (U and V), spanning a radial range of 77.41–213.922 cm.  Three SMD
 * section groups define the strip pattern across the azimuthal supersectors.
 *
 * ### Simulation versions
 * - **ECALGEO (version 5.0)** — original production geometry by Mehdiyev (1996).
 *   The `onoff` parameter controls which endcap(s) are instantiated (1=west, 2=east, 3=both).
 *   The `fillmode` parameter controls whether both (3) or one (1) φ half-wheel is filled.
 * - **ECALGEO6 (version 6.1)** — updated geometry adding ECUT / EABS / ESEN structures for
 *   per-material configurable EM transport cuts; also adds EMCS geometry version 2 with a
 *   tie-rod radius parameter (Rtie) and cell-size correction (Slop).  Production geometry for
 *   Run 9 and beyond.
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @file EcalGeo.xml
 * @brief Module ECALGEO — endcap EMC geometry version 5.0 (1996).
 *
 * Core structures:
 * - **EMCG** — version, on/off, fillmode switches
 * - **EMCS** — full calorimeter geometry (z positions, η/φ extents, plate thicknesses)
 * - **EETR** — η binning: 12 η bins from 1.086 to 2.0
 * - **ESEC** (×5) — per-section layer counts and cell widths
 * - **EMXG** — SMD strip apex/base/radius parameters
 * - **EXSE** (×3) — SMD section U/V/cut-strip assignments
 *
 * Sensitive volumes: ESCI (tower scintillator), EHMS (SMD triangular strip).
 */

/**
 * @file EcalGeo6.xml
 * @brief Module ECALGEO6 — endcap EMC geometry version 6.1 with configurable EM cuts.
 *
 * Extends ECALGEO by adding:
 * - **ECUT** — boolean switches for absorber and sensitive volume cuts
 * - **EABS** — GEANT3 transport thresholds for absorbing material (CutGAM, CutELE, …)
 * - **ESEN** — corresponding thresholds for the sensitive scintillator
 * - **EMCS version 2** — adds tie-rod radius (Rtie = 1.0425 cm) and cell-size
 *   correction (Slop = 0.14 cm) parameters
 * - Additional SMD structural blocks: EFLS, EBLS (front/back layer material slabs),
 *   EXPS (plastic spacer between SMD planes)
 *
 * ECALv6 enables EM cuts (absorber=1, sensitive=1); ECALv6_cut00 disables both.
 */

/**
 * @file EcalConfig.xml
 * @brief Setup registry for detector ECAL.
 *
 * | Setup | Module | onoff | fillmode | Notes |
 * |---|---|---|---|---|
 * | ECALof | EcalGeo | — | — | disabled |
 * | ECALon | EcalGeo | 1 | 3 | west, full φ |
 * | ECAL31 | EcalGeo | 1 | 3 | same as ECALon |
 * | ECAL11 | EcalGeo | 1 | 1 | west, one half |
 * | ECAL33 | EcalGeo | 3 | 3 | both endcaps |
 * | ECALv6 | EcalGeo6 | 1 | 3 | v6, cuts on |
 * | ECALv6_cut00 | EcalGeo6 | 1 | 3 | v6, cuts off |
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
